 <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic">Hotel guests travel with multiple devices and increasingly expect charging to be part of the room, not an afterthought. In-room charging capability influences guest satisfaction and online ratings. For procurement teams, the question is not whether to install charging amenities, but which technology mix delivers the best utility per room category: Qi2 wireless, GaN USB-C, or portable power banks.</p>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mt-4">The global wireless charging market is projected to reach <strong>$31.6 billion by 2030</strong> (CAGR 24.2%), with hospitality as a growth vertical, according to Grand View Research. According to the <strong>J.D. Power 2025 North America Hotel Guest Satisfaction Index (NAGSI)</strong>, room amenities and technology are top drivers of guest satisfaction. In that study, 72% of guests reported having a smart TV in their room, up from 39% in 2019, a sign of how quickly in-room technology expectations rise.</p>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mt-4">The EU <strong>Common Charger Directive 2022/2380</strong> mandates USB-C across member states from December 2024, directly impacting hotel charger procurement for European properties. At WOWOHCOOL, we build GaN chargers and Qi2-certified wireless solutions designed for the hospitality industry.</p>
