 <p class="text-badge font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Key Takeaways</p>
 <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4 speakable">Hotel in-room charging improves guest satisfaction and reduces front-desk charging requests. A bedside Qi2 dock with dual USB-C ports covers most overnight charging needs. Hotel-grade specs are non-negotiable: fixed or retractable cables, V-0 fire-rated enclosures for insurance compliance, and 100-240V input for international guests. OEM branding at MOQ 500 units adds $0.30-0.80/unit and puts your hotel name on a high-use amenity.</p>
 <ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
 <li><strong>In-room charging is a high-visibility amenity</strong>. Hotels that deploy multi-device GaN charging stations can see higher guest satisfaction scores and fewer front-desk "do you have a charger?" requests. A modest per-room investment pays back through review ratings and repeat stays.</li>
 <li><strong>3 charger form factors dominate hotel deployments</strong>: (1) bedside alarm-clock-style with integrated wireless pad + 2 USB-C ports (most popular, $9-14 FOB at 500+ units), (2) desk-mount multi-port GaN hub (65-100W, $6-10 FOB), (3) lobby/public area floor-standing kiosk with retractable cables ($18-28 FOB). The bedside unit delivers 80% of guest utility, start there.</li>
 <li><strong>Hotel procurement requirements differ from consumer retail</strong>: (1) fixed cable or retractable (detachable cables are easily lost or taken), (2) tamper-resistant mounting (screw-down or adhesive to furniture), (3) universal voltage (100-240V for international guests), (4) fire-rated enclosure (hotel insurance requires V-0 flammability rating). Consumer-grade chargers often fail on these points.</li>
 <li><strong>OEM branding for hotels: laser-engraved logo + room number on each unit</strong>. Standard MOQ 500 units per model (laser engraving); 1,000 units for silk-screen logos. Custom branding adds $0.30-0.80/unit. Branded units are less likely to be taken and create a premium guest touchpoint.</li>
 </ul>
