 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">1. Guest Room Wireless Charging: Qi2 Bedside Docks for Hospitality</h2>
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">What is the difference between Qi2, Qi, and MagSafe for hotels?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Qi2 is the Wireless Power Consortium standard for magnetic wireless charging, using the same magnet array as Apple MagSafe and delivering up to 15W. Qi is the older inductive standard without magnetic alignment. MagSafe is Apple's proprietary implementation for iPhone. For hotels, specify Qi2-certified products so guests with iPhone and Android devices both get reliable alignment; "Qi compatible" without certification is not enough.</p>
 <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4 leading-relaxed">Hotel guests often forget their charging cables. Or they find the cable is too short for the bedside outlet. This is a common frustration. But it is easy to fix.</p>

 <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6">
