 <!-- FAQ -->
 <section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What type of chargers should hotel procurement teams deploy per room zone?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Three form factors cover all hotel deployment zones: (1) <strong>bedside Qi2 3-in-1 wireless dock</strong> with integrated USB-C ports, the highest-utility unit at <strong>$9-14 FOB at 500+ units</strong>, covering 80% of guest charging needs; (2) <strong>desk-mount multi-port GaN hub</strong> at 65-100W with 2C1A configuration at $6-10 FOB; (3) <strong>lobby/public area floor-standing kiosk</strong> with retractable cables at $18-28 FOB. For hotel shuttle fleets, USB-C PD car chargers at $8-12 FOB cover guest transport. Start with bedside units per room, then add desk and lobby units based on guest feedback and budget cycles.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Qi2 vs GaN vs standard USB-C, which charger technology fits which hotel deployment zone?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Bedside: Qi2 wireless 3-in-1 dock</strong>, Best for guest rooms. Charges phone + watch + earbuds simultaneously without cable clutter. 15W Qi2 MPP with N52H magnets ensures reliable alignment. <strong>Desk: GaN multi-port hub 65-100W</strong>, Best for business travelers who need laptop + phone charging at a workstation. Compact size with high power output in 2C1A configuration. <strong>Lobby: floor-standing kiosk</strong>, Best for high-traffic shared areas. Needs retractable cables and durable construction rated for 5,000+ insertions. <strong>Shuttle: USB-C PD car charger 30-45W</strong>, Best for guest transport. Dual-port with PPS for Samsung and iPhone fast charging. All four technologies can be sourced from a single OEM manufacturer for consistent branding and warranty terms across deployment zones.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What certifications must hotel chargers have for EU and US hospitality compliance?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Mandatory for EU hotels:</strong> CE marking (LVD 2014/35/EU + EMC 2014/30/EU), RoHS 2011/65/EU, and compliance with the EU Common Charger Directive 2022/2380 (USB-C mandate from December 2024). Hotel-specific: EN 62368-1:2020/A11:2020 for audio/video and ICT safety in commercial environments.</p>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Mandatory for US hotels:</strong> FCC Part 15B, UL 62368-1 (ANSI/UL 62368-1 3rd Ed.), and NFPA 70 (NEC 2023) Article 406 for receptacle installations.</p>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Both markets require:</strong> Qi2 certification from WPC, verify in the WPC Certified Product Database at wirelesspowerconsortium.com. "Qi compatible" without certification is insufficient for commercial deployment. Additionally: UL 94 V-0 flame rating (hotel insurer requirement), IEC 61000-4-5 surge immunity, and IP54 minimum enclosure rating (EN 60529) for bathroom-adjacent bedside units.</p>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Energy management:</strong> ASHRAE 90.1 (current edition) Section 8.4 for hotel receptacle load calculations, and ISO 50001:2018 for chain-wide energy management system certification.</p>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">WOWOHCOOL ships every hotel order with a pre-assembled compliance binder. It contains UL/CE/FCC certificates per SKU, UN38.3 test reports, ISO 9001 certificate, and WPC Qi2 certification, organized for corporate procurement and legal review.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What MOQ and FOB pricing apply to custom-branded hotel chargers at OEM volume?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Standard MOQ for hotel-branded chargers: <strong>500 units per model</strong> for ODM in-stock customization (laser engraving; 1,000 for silk-screen logos). MOQ is not pooled across different product categories. FOB Shenzhen pricing at 500+ units per model: Qi2 bedside dock $9-14/unit, GaN multi-port hub $6-10/unit, lobby kiosk $18-28/unit, car charger $8-12/unit. Custom branding adds <strong>$0.30-0.80/unit</strong> for laser-engraved logo with room number. Prices decline 8-15% at 1,000+ units.</p>
 </div>



 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do hotel procurement managers start an OEM order for branded chargers with phased deployment?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Start with a free consultation: specify your property count, rooms per property, deployment zones (bedside, desk, lobby, shuttle), and desired branding method. WOWOHCOOL provides a phased deployment proposal with bulk pricing tiers, compliance documentation per SKU, and category-based warranty terms (12 months for wireless chargers and power banks, 24 months for GaN and car chargers). <strong>Request 3 production-grade samples</strong> for in-room testing before committing to a full order, test with actual guests for 2-4 weeks and collect housekeeping feedback. Payment terms: 30% deposit, 70% before shipment, with DDP delivery options available. <strong>First-time hotel buyers receive a pre-assembled compliance binder and housekeeping training guide with every order. <a href="/contact/" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange underline">Contact WOWOHCOOL for a custom hospitality quote</a> with current FOB pricing and lead times.</strong></p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>


